(1408887, 180601, 37249, '<td valign="top">This is what lightning is all about. One need not have digitally "made over" photographs... good lightning, good lightning and good lightning do make this a winner. And oh, yes, nice colors and proper use of depth of field are also great in this picture.</td>', 'This is what lightning is all about. One need not have digitally "made over" photographs... good lightning, good lightning and good lightning do make this a winner. And oh, yes, nice colors and proper use of depth of field are also great in this picture.', '2005-05-24 17:49:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1408890, 179910, 24642, '<td valign="top">One of the best in the challenge.  I really like lighting both from above and in the background.   The profile view works well with the lighting you choose.  The choice of background and border is very fitting.  -10</td>', 'One of the best in the challenge.  I really like lighting both from above and in the background.   The profile view works well with the lighting you choose.  The choice of background and border is very fitting.  -10', '2005-05-24 17:51:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1408892, 181010, 3032, '<td valign="top">Hi ''Cherie'',<br/> <br/>Stumbled onto this photo at pbase earlier this evening. Wanted to leave a comment there later, I also like that shot of the field with the tree a lot. But now I see it again here.<br/> <br/>This one is great, the symmetry and soft colors are very entertaining. Perhaps the top part is hurt by overexposure around the edges, creating some softness and strange color effects on the rose petals, but that is not so important here.<br/>The rose looks like it bends down to have a good look at itself. What it finds is a kind of blue dreamworld. The shades and tones of blue there are wonderful (the color blue is my fav color).<br/>No matter how I twist my head, I like what I see. :)<br/>Good luck!</td>', 'Hi ''Cherie'', Stumbled onto this photo at pbase earlier this evening. Wanted to leave a comment there later, I also like that shot of the field with the tree a lot. But now I see it again here. This one is great, the symmetry and soft colors are very entertaining. Perhaps the top part is hurt by overexposure around the edges, creating some softness and strange color effects on the rose petals, but that is not so important here.The rose looks like it bends down to have a good look at itself. What it finds is a kind of blue dreamworld. The shades and tones of blue there are wonderful (the color blue is my fav color).No matter how I twist my head, I like what I see. :)Good luck!', '2005-05-24 17:52:03.000000', NULL, 1),
